 -- NostrHost <nostrhost@example.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:45:00 +0000

yunohost (12.1.41.110) stable; urgency=low

  * operations read-path performance: `list_operations` and `get_operation`
    no longer replay the whole operation chain for every request.
    `list_operations` reads a bounded window (the newest `limit` kind-2200
    requests plus their follow-ons, matched by `#e`) with a 3-second server
    cache, so the admin console's ~15s polling and Home-overview load are
    deduped and the relay REQ cost tracks the requested page size instead of
    the chain length. `get_operation` fetches one request's chain by
    `ids`/`#e` instead of the entire list. Kind-2205 progress events are
    excluded from these reads (the state reduction never transitions on
    them). `query_chain_events` gains `ids`/`e_tags` filter support. This
    fixes the console's operations screen timing out after 30s ("Failed to
    load operations") on a grown chain.

