 -- NostrHost <nostrhost@example.com>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 03:00:00 +0000

yunohost (12.1.41.104) stable; urgency=low

  * fix: replay guard now treats a request that already published
    execution_started (2203) as non-rerunnable on a fresh-connect replay.
    Previously only requests with a terminal 2204 result were marked
    executed, so an op that was interrupted mid-execution by an executor
    restart (e.g. an approved `service.restart nostr-operationsd` kills the
    daemon before it publishes its own result) was re-run on every replay —
    for a self-restart op that is an infinite restart loop. `_mark_terminal_results`
    now marks every id that published 2203, so the replayed request and its
    approval are no-ops and the daemon stays up (the interrupted op is left
    without a terminal result and must be re-submitted). Regression test:
    test_restart_replay_does_not_reexecute_midflight_request.

