    resolves approval/rejection authority at decision time from the signer's
    enabled identity and current membership of the native admins group, so
    group removal and identity revocation take effect immediately without a
    daemon restart or a second stale pubkey allowlist. Configured operator
    keys remain a bootstrap fallback, and the store fails closed. The
    owner-co-signature special case is removed: any current admin's signed
    decision is the approval. The control relay defers 2201/2202 writer policy
    to the executor, and the API reports a submitted decision as
    status:"submitted" (relay acknowledgement only, not executor acceptance).

